{"id": "8", "question": "What is the product of all solutions to the equation\n\\[\\log_{7x}2023\\cdot \\log_{289x}2023=\\log_{2023x}2023\\]", "gold_answer": "1", "n_traces": 8, "n_correct_traces": 1, "bon_correct": true, "dnbon_correct": false, "oracle_correct": true, "majority_correct": false, "bon_answer": "1", "dnbon_answer": "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{119}", "bon_raw_score": 0.6875, "dnbon_raw_score": 0.554688, "dnbon_norm_score": 0.554688, "dnbon_cluster_size": 1, "fmax": 0.875, "H": 0.543564443196711, "He": 0.18118814773223701, "M": 2, "r": 0.25, "multiplicity_bias_fired": false, "prm_scores": [0.484375, 0.554688, 0.154297, 0.535156, 0.009155, 0.133789, 0.166016, 0.6875], "cluster_labels": [0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], "cluster_sizes_all": [7, 1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7], "cimr_full_correct": false, "cimr_full_answer": "\\sqrt{\\frac{2023}{7}}", "cimr_full_raw_response": "(7x)^y\\). Similarly, let \\(z = \\log_{289x}2023\\), so \\(2023 = (289x)^z\\), and let \\(w = \\log_{2023x}2023\\), so \\(2023 = (2023x)^w\\). The given equation is \\(y \\cdot z = w\\).\n\nFrom \\(2023 = (7x)^y\\), we have \\(y = \\frac{\\ln 2023}{\\ln (7x)}\\). From \\(2023 = (289x)^z\\), we have \\(z = \\frac{\\ln 2023}{\\ln (289x)}\\). From \\(2023 = (2023x)^w\\), we have \\(w = \\frac{\\ln 2023}{\\ln (2023x)}\\).\n\nSubstituting these into the equation \\(y \\cdot z = w\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\ln 2023}{\\ln (7x)} \\cdot \\frac{\\ln 2023}{\\ln (289x)} = \\frac{\\ln 2023}{\\ln (2023x)}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\ln 2023 \\neq 0\\), we can divide both sides by \\(\\ln 2023\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\ln (7x)} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\ln (289x)} = \\frac{1}{\\ln (2023x)}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\ln (7x) \\ln (289x)} = \\frac{1}{\\ln (2023x)}\n\\]\n\nTaking the reciprocals of both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\ln (7x) \\ln (289x) = \\ln (2023x)\n\\]\n\nUsing the properties of logarithms, we can expand both sides:\n\n\\[\n\\ln 7 + \\ln x \\cdot \\ln 289 + \\ln x = \\ln 2023 + \\ln x\n\\]\n\nSubtracting \\(\\ln x\\) from both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\ln 7 + \\ln x \\cdot \\ln 289 = \\ln 2023\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms to isolate \\(\\ln x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\ln x \\cdot \\ln 289 = \\ln 2023 - \\ln 7\n\\]\n\nUsing the property of logarithms that \\(\\ln a - \\ln b = \\ln \\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)\\), we can rewrite the right side as:\n\n\\[\n\\ln x \\cdot \\ln 289 = \\ln \\left(\\frac{2023}{7}\\right)\n\\]\n\nSince \\(289 = 17^2\\), we have \\(\\ln 289 = \\ln (17^2) = 2 \\ln 17\\). Substituting this in, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\ln x \\cdot 2 \\ln 17 = \\ln \\left(\\frac{2023}{7}\\right)\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(\\ln x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\ln x = \\frac{\\ln \\left(\\frac{2023}{7}\\right)}{2 \\ln 17}\n\\]\n\nExponentiating both sides to solve for \\(x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nx = e^{\\frac{\\ln \\left(\\frac{2023}{7}\\right)}{2 \\ln 17}} = \\left(e^{\\ln \\left(\\frac{2023}{7}\\right)}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2 \\ln 17}} = \\left(\\frac{2023}{7}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2 \\ln 17}}\n\\]\n\nThe product of all solutions to the equation is simply the solution itself, which is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{\\frac{2023}{7}}}\n\\]", "cimr_concise_correct": false, "cimr_concise_answer": "17", "cimr_concise_raw_response": "3}(7x)} = \\frac{1}{\\log_{2023}7 + \\log_{2023}x}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\log_{289x}2023 = \\frac{\\log_{2023}2023}{\\log_{2023}(289x)} = \\frac{1}{\\log_{2023}289 + \\log_{2023}x} = \\frac{1}{2 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}x}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\log_{2023x}2023 = \\frac{\\log_{2023}2023}{\\log_{2023}(2023x)} = \\frac{1}{\\log_{2023}2023 + \\log_{2023}x} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\log_{2023}x}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these into the original equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\log_{2023}7 + \\log_{2023}x} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}x} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\log_{2023}x}\n\\]\n\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\\[\n(1 + \\log_{2023}x) \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\log_{2023}7 + \\log_{2023}x} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}x} = 1\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{1 + \\log_{2023}x}{(\\log_{2023}7 + \\log_{2023}x)(2 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}x)} = 1\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by \\((\\log_{2023}7 + \\log_{2023}x)(2 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}x)\\), we get:\n\\[\n1 + \\log_{2023}x = (\\log_{2023}7 + \\log_{2023}x)(2 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}x)\n\\]\n\nExpanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\\[\n1 + \\log_{2023}x = 2 \\log_{2023}7 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}7 \\log_{2023}x + 2 \\log_{2023}17 \\log_{2023}x + \\log_{2023}x^2\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n1 + \\log_{2023}x = \\log_{2023}x^2 + 3 \\log_{2023}7 \\log_{2023}17 + \\log_{2023}7 \\log_{2023}x + 2 \\log_{2023}17 \\log_{2023}x\n\\]\n\nSubtracting \\(\\log_{2023}x\\) from both sides, we get:\n\\[\n1 = \\log_{2023}x^2 + 3 \\log_{2023}7 \\log_{2023}17 + 2 \\log_{2023}7 \\log_{2023}x + \\log_{2023}17 \\log_{2023}x\n\\]\n\nThis equation is satisfied when \\(x = 17\\). Therefore, the product of all solutions is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{17}\n\\]"}
